  clock: 6  # b6eb
  nonce: b6eb  # b6eb
  message: "STAGE 4 MERGED, PR #1180 (+ tracker #1181). STATUS: STAYS VIOLATED, on 9 typescript edges with a different cause, now tracked as WI-pizan (isbefore this item).\n\nWHERE EVERY FILED LANGUAGE STANDS, re-measured on the INV-midag repos with surveys from pinned worktrees, calls edges, analyzer origin:\n  kotlin 2014 -> 0, scala 964 -> 0, swift 273 -> 0   (#1176, position-keyed lookup)\n  c 35 -> 0, rust 5 -> 0, ruby 3 -> 0, csharp 3 -> 0 (#1177)\n  haskell 119 -> 0                                    (#1178: the SPAN was short, not the anchor)\n  javascript 135 -> 0, typescript 33 -> 9             (#1180)\n  go: a second `func init()` in one file was mis-anchored. That was invisible on gin and logrus and found by fixture. Fixed in #1180.\n  java: verified clean with an overload fixture. elixir and erlang: INV-mozas.\n\nTHE 9: all in koel's components/utils/HotkeyListener.vue. Its anonymous-callback symbols are positioned WITHOUT the .vue <script> line_offset while their calls carry it. That is WI-pizan's mechanism, not the name lookup this item is about. The title condition (\"violated in ... TS\") still holds for them, so this item is not closed.\n\nTHE GATE the row asked for: test_call_anchor_gate.py (lang-mainstream), _common and _extended1. They enumerate from source all 42 analyzer modules that define an enclosing lookup. 13 are VERIFIED against a named, executing containment test. 29 are UNVERIFIED against WI-mapor. A new analyzer with a lookup and no classification fails the gate. The UNVERIFIED half is bookkeeping, and the docstrings say so.\n\nSIDE FINDINGS FILED: WI-tisom (P2, the noise filter drops swift/C# properties); WI-pizan (P3, .vue callback offset); WI-mapor (P3, 29 unverified analyzers).\n\nNOT ASSERTED: the general statement for the 29 unverified analyzers, or for any language on repositories outside this corpus."  # b6eb
